WEBVTT

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:11.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday 30 July. Can you hear me all right? Teams is doing that spinning thing again.</v>

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:16.089
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, you're through. Anyone see the football last night?</v>

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.969
<v David Whitfield>Unfortunately. There's ninety minutes I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:25.140
<v Marcus Hale>Oh, come on, last ten minutes were decent.</v>

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:29.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, pundits off. We're all here, are we?</v>

00:00:31.309 --> 00:00:36.909
<v Priya Raman>I'm here. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid, so I've only just sat down.</v>

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:43.840
<v Callum Reid>Same. Think I spent longer looking at the gate than driving the rest of it.</v>

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:52.259
<v Priya Raman>And then the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Lovely start. That's a moan, by the way, not me volunteering to fix it.</v>

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:56.229
<v Grace Liu>Cold tea's available if you fancy a different disappointment.</v>

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:02.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Living the dream. Let's get the finished bits out of the way first.</v>

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:09.549
<v Priya Raman>Yeah so, tested the Boiler Safety Relief Valve yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:14.269
<v David Whitfield>That's the one that was still showing open on the list?</v>

00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:19.219
<v Priya Raman>Yep, that one. Finished yesterday, nothing new off the back of it.</v>

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:25.620
<v David Whitfield>And I signed off the inspection on the number two bearing on Tuesday. That's finished as well.</v>

00:01:26.959 --> 00:01:30.109
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Both closed, not rolling them into today's jobs.</v>

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:37.299
<v Grace Liu>Same sort of update from me: tested the AC1 yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:43.379
<v Callum Reid>Right, cheers. I wasn't sure whether that was an old entry.</v>

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:49.980
<v Grace Liu>It was. Separate thing, I heard a slight rattle from the 11kV Switchboard, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:55.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Just an observation at this point, then? Not a job you're asking anyone to take?</v>

00:01:57.859 --> 00:01:59.260
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Just an observation.</v>

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:06.469
<v Grace Liu>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the compressor one. That's still blocked, I'm afraid.</v>

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, still sitting as blocked in the schedule. No confirmed delivery to plan around.</v>

00:02:15.139 --> 00:02:20.740
<v Callum Reid>While we're on blocked things, can't get to the Palletiser until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:26.030
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's not being handed out as a fresh job this morning.</v>

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:29.639
<v Callum Reid>No. Just explaining why it hasn't moved.</v>

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:38.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Marc, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the Injection Moulding Line 2 this morning? That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:40.539 --> 00:02:46.490
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Injection Moulding Line 2 this morning.</v>

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.860
<v Grace Liu>Sorry, talked over the end there. This morning was the permit and isolation, yeah?</v>

00:02:52.719 --> 00:02:58.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, that whole bit this morning. Fairly important, so not one to leave in the odds-and-ends pile.</v>

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.650
<v Marcus Hale>Got you. That's mine.</v>

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:09.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, the other one for you: can you sort the training records for the new starters, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:03:11.509 --> 00:03:17.110
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll sort the training records for the new starters. Whenever I get a chance, understood.</v>

00:03:18.199 --> 00:03:20.650
<v Fiona Doyle>No fixed deadline on the records, then?</v>

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:26.139
<v Sarah Okafor>No fixed deadline. That's the whenever-you-get-a-chance one, not the same urgency as the permit.</v>

00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:30.939
<v Marcus Hale>Fine, yeah. Two separate things, I've got them.</v>

00:03:32.449 --> 00:03:37.000
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, could you book a contractor to look at the fire alarm panel?</v>

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:46.280
<v Priya Raman>Yep—sorry, just making sure: you're asking me to make the booking, not saying the contractor has to be here this morning?</v>

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:54.300
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, book a contractor to look at it. I'm not putting a visit deadline on that.</v>

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:59.289
<v Priya Raman>Okay, I'll book a contractor to look at the fire alarm panel.</v>

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.909
<v David Whitfield>Not the coffee machine contractor, before anyone gets their hopes up.</v>

00:04:06.169 --> 00:04:09.319
<v Priya Raman>Definitely not. My coffee complaint remains strictly a complaint.</v>

00:04:09.729 --> 00:04:14.629
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll order spare parts for the CT1 next week. No rush on that one.</v>

00:04:16.819 --> 00:04:21.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah against the CT1 spare parts, next week, no rush. Got it.</v>

00:04:23.019 --> 00:04:26.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's mine. Next week, not an urgent order.</v>

00:04:28.529 --> 00:04:31.680
<v Marcus Hale>Right, good. Not another thing in this morning's scramble.</v>

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:41.819
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll send the shift handover report round on the 3rd. That's very much in the 'if you've got a spare minute' category, not an urgent one.</v>

00:04:43.879 --> 00:04:47.730
<v Fiona Doyle>Saz for the shift handover report, on the 3rd, low priority?</v>

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, exactly. I'll do that.</v>

00:04:53.069 --> 00:05:03.920
<v Grace Liu>Um, there is still the near miss at the line 2 robot to write up, on the 3rd. It needs doing, but I'm raising the gap here, not taking the write-up.</v>

00:05:05.759 --> 00:05:08.209
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I haven't taken that one either.</v>

00:05:09.519 --> 00:05:14.069
<v David Whitfield>Nor me. Don't put it against me just because I've come off mute.</v>

00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:17.949
<v Fiona Doyle>So that's genuinely no owner at the moment?</v>

00:05:20.389 --> 00:05:27.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Write up the near miss at the line 2 robot, on the 3rd, but unallocated. Nobody's agreed to take it.</v>

00:05:29.189 --> 00:05:34.089
<v Grace Liu>Thanks. Just didn't want it looking like an HSE commitment because I'd mentioned it.</v>

00:05:34.649 --> 00:05:39.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Quick check before we go: Marc, permit and isolation this morning, fairly important.</v>

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:47.069
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, agreed. And the new starters' training records whenever I get a chance. Haven't mixed those up.</v>

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:53.279
<v Priya Raman>And I've got the contractor booking for the fire alarm panel.</v>

00:05:54.209 --> 00:06:00.160
<v Fiona Doyle>Near miss still has a blank owner, though. That's the outstanding gap, not silently sitting with anyone.</v>

00:06:00.769 --> 00:06:01.970
<v Grace Liu>Exactly, yes.</v>

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks all. That's the stand-up. I'll let you get on.</v>

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:10.500
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely. Back to arguing about the football, then.</v>

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.000
<v Priya Raman>Without coffee? You're on your own, mate.</v>
